---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy, SyncSet"
  description="How SyncSet collects, uses and protects the personal information you share with us, and how to contact us about it."
>
  <Header />

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="legal">
      <div class="legal__container">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal__updated">Last updated: 14 September 2026</p>

        <p>
          SyncSet ("we", "us", "our") operates syncset.com.au. This page explains what personal information we collect through this site, why, and what you can do about it.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          When you submit the contact form or book a workflow audit, we collect your name, email address, business name, and anything you write in the message field. If you book a call through the "Book a Workflow Audit" button, our scheduling provider collects your name, email address, and the time you select.
        </p>
        <p>
          We don't collect payment information through this site.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use it</h2>
        <p>
          We use this information to respond to your enquiry, run the workflow audit, and follow up about our services. We don't use it for unrelated marketing without your separate consent, and we don't sell or rent it to anyone.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it goes</h2>
        <p>
          An enquiry submitted through the contact form on this site is sent to Make.com, our automation platform, which routes it into our CRM (Notion) and sends an internal alert to our own Telegram notification bot so we see it immediately. This is the same pipeline described under "How it works" on the homepage. It's what runs our own business, too.
        </p>
        <p>
          A booking made through the "Book a Workflow Audit" button is handled directly by Cal.com, a third-party scheduling service that collects and processes your details under its own privacy policy; we don't control how it stores that data.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because these providers operate outside Australia, your information may be processed on servers overseas (the EU, for Make.com; the United States, for Notion and Cal.com). We only use providers who publish their own data-protection commitments.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We keep enquiry data for as long as needed to respond to you and, if you become a client, for the length of our working relationship plus a reasonable period to meet our accounting and legal obligations. If you don't become a client, we delete or anonymise your enquiry data after 12 months.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the personal information we hold about you at any time; email <a href="mailto:contact@syncset.com.au">contact@syncset.com.au</a>. We'll respond within a reasonable time.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless and collects no personal data. The Cal.com booking widget, if you use it, may set its own cookies under its own policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy as our tools or process change. The date at the top shows the last revision.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:contact@syncset.com.au">contact@syncset.com.au</a>, Byron Bay NSW 2481, Australia.
        </p>

        <p class="legal__disclaimer">
          <strong>⚠️ Note:</strong> This draft was prepared by Claude, not a lawyer, from SyncSet's actual data flow; it is not legal advice. Before publishing, confirm: whether SyncSet's turnover keeps it under the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) small-business exemption threshold (currently A$3 million) and, if so, whether voluntary compliance is still the right call for client trust; whether the overseas-disclosure wording (Australian Privacy Principle 8) matches the actual terms in effect with Make.com, Notion, and Cal.com; and whether the 12-month retention period matches what you actually intend to do operationally.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    min-height: calc(100vh - 200px);
    padding: var(--space-24) var(--gutter);
    background-color: var(--paper);
  }

  .legal__container {
    max-width: var(--max-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--graphite);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .legal__container h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal__updated {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--graphite);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  .legal__container h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .legal__container p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .legal__container strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .legal__container a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .legal__disclaimer {
    margin-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .legal {
      padding: var(--space-16) var(--gutter);
    }

    .legal__container h1 {
      font-size: var(--text-xl);
    }
  }
</style>
